title: >-
  FlashSpec: Adaptive Speculative Decoding with Online Bandit Draft
  Selection and Triton-Optimised Verification
authors:
  - family-names: Myet
    given-names: "Min Htet"
    alias: Mattral
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-0853-8301"
abstract: >-
  FlashSpec is an open-source adaptive speculative-decoding inference
  engine for large language models. It implements token verification
  with a Triton kernel and a pure-PyTorch reference, and can select
  among registered drafters with UCB1 or Thompson sampling. The suite
  checks the output distribution with a chi-squared test. That test is
  not a continuous-integration gate in this revision. Committed
  end-to-end pairs are slower than autoregressive decoding.
